      "index": 0,
      "text": " <think>\nTo solve the problem of finding the product of 97 and 91, we can use the standard multiplication method. This involves multiplying each digit of one number by each digit of the other number and then adding the results. However, for simplicity, we can also use the difference of squares formula if we recognize a pattern. Let's break it down step by step.\n</think>\n<answer>\nFirst, let's calculate the product directly using the standard multiplication method:\n\\[ 97 \\times 91 \\]\nWe can break this down into:\n\\[ (100 - 3) \\times (100 - 9) \\]\nUsing the distributive property (also known as the FOIL method for binomials):\n\\[ (100 - 3)(100 - 9) = 100 \\times 100 - 100 \\times 9 - 3 \\times 100 + 3 \\times 9 \\]\n\\[ = 10000 - 900 - 300 + 27 \\]\n\\[ = 10000 - 1200 + 27 \\]\n\\[ = 8800 + 27 \\]\n\\[ = 8827 \\]\nSo, the product of 97 and 91 is 8827.\n</answer>",
